/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529138 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2+y-x}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-2x}{6}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529138 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "72ca9ca6-7469-59a8-9b29-546c35450d5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529138 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2+y-x}{3})}{(\\frac{5-2x}{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2+y-x)}{5-2x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2(2+y-1)}{5-2\\cdot 1}=\\frac{2(1+y)}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\cdot \\frac{2(1+y)}{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y+{y}^{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529166 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529166 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146256" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529166 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529166 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+y)}{4}, & 0<x\\le 2y,\\,\\,0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}, & 0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529166 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0901d8a-5ab9-5481-aeea-fb9811603032" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529166 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3(x+y)}{4})}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+y)}{4{y}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<x\\le 2y,\\,0<y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$ \n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{(x+1)}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{(x+1)}{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(\\frac{8}{3}+2)-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529196 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186529032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529196 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146344" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529196 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529196 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1+y-x, & 0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,\\,0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529196 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "febf3d13-3a80-5fb8-bb8d-fc4ac7755bf9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529196 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1+y-x)}{2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 2y,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$ \n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{(2-x)}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the definition of the conditional expectation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{(2-x)}{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(4-\\frac{8}{3})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529198 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529198 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1181624e-c0cd-5f60-b961-039085d0722f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529198 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186529166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529201 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529201 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a211e675-f3f3-58f6-9ae3-cb834095d76e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529201 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186529196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529202 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a56c8877-9613-5958-b79a-c092e65fd1f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529202 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186529138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529205 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186529198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529205 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e99a2b96-04a4-56d4-b984-c2f3490f6093" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186529205 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162414 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
